  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "I0abUuOFNH6N/efiKq8P31ONlDU=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:44:22.975Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`packages/document-model/README.md` opens with:\n\n```\nnpm install @acaldas/document-model-libs\n```\n\nand documents interaction with a document through imports like `@acaldas/document-model-libs/budget-statement`, pointing at `acaldas.github.io/document-model-libs` for full documentation.\n\nThat is the package's pre-Powerhouse identity. The directory now publishes **`document-model`**, which is what every current import in the monorepo and in generated projects uses \u2014 including the `document-model/mock` subpath that the Academy's test tutorials were corrected to at this tag.\n\nWhat is still useful in the file is the *shape* it teaches: a document can be driven **functionally** (`actions`, `reducer`, `utils` \u2014 `utils.createDocument(...)` then `reducer(doc, actions.addAccount(...))`) as well as through a class-style controller. That functional triple is exactly what generated document models still export.\n\nThe reading rule: take the API shape, ignore every package name and URL in it. A newcomer following its install line gets an unrelated, unmaintained package.\n\n## Provenance\n- `packages/document-model/README.md` \u2014 Getting started (install line and docs link); Functional example\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:44:22.975Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:44:22.975Z"
    }
  },
